- op: discuss  # 10d2
  at: '2026-10-31T23:30:02Z'  # 10d2
  by: agent  # 10d2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 10d2
  clock: 2  # 10d2
  nonce: 10d2  # 10d2
  message: "Fix committed on local branch jgstern-agent/fix/vahun as c352cb51f6. Not pushed; the integrator handles it. The premise reproduced on dev 217890b1aa: in the item's fixture, both include edges were dangling with is_resolved=False. Fix: PuppetAnalyzer now runs on TreeSitterAnalyzer's two-pass template methods. Pass 1 declares symbols; the base registers ALL files' classes; Pass 2 resolves includes and emits require/notify edges. After the fix, beta binds to puppet:a.pp:5-6:beta:class and zeta to puppet:z.pp:1-2:zeta:class, both is_resolved=True. An old/new dump of a 2-file fixture shows identical symbols and edges, except the 2 forward includes. Tests: 7 property tests. RED 4 failed on dev; GREEN 11444 passed with changed files at 100%; a mutation that restores the declared-so-far registry fails 5 of them. Side effect of the base pipeline: an empty repo returns a run with files_analyzed=0, not run=None. Corpus A/B was not possible: no corpus repo contains Puppet (the 21 .pp files are compiled SELinux policies). Related defects filed: WI-hozot-lahub-tazis-gozap-galad-lokat-himof-hidab (namespaced class a::b never extracted; include lists and quoted includes drop names; these keep real-world includes unbound in any order) and WI-zotoh-sagod-jifiz-tamoj-hosar-kobup-vuboz-hafap (the same order-dependence in scss and svelte)."  # 10d2
