- op: discuss  # 96df
  at: '2026-11-01T02:26:27Z'  # 96df
  by: agent  # 96df
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 96df
  clock: 4  # 96df
  nonce: 96df  # 96df
  message: "Fixed in PR #1983 (a48300e738 and d834645220 on dev). Root cause: one sequential walk both filled _class_registry and read it, so an include saw only classes declared earlier. Puppet now runs the base TreeSitterAnalyzer two-pass pipeline: Pass 1 records every file, classes are registered before Pass 2 resolves includes. The integration full suite caught a meta write the meta-key scan could not enumerate; it is now a literal (d834645220). Live repro on merged dev: hypergumbo survey on the item fixture (class alpha { include beta include zeta }, beta lower in a.pp, zeta in z.pp): rc=0, includes target puppet:a.pp:5-6:beta:class and puppet:z.pp:1-2:zeta:class, both real nodes (before: two unresolved dangling edges). Tests: 7 in test_puppet.py (4 red before). Residuals filed: WI-hozot (namespaced classes not extracted, multi-name include), WI-zotoh (SCSS and lang-common Svelte order dependence)."  # 96df
